---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { getManifest } from "../lib/content";
const m = getManifest();
const synced = new Date(m.syncedAt).toUTCString().replace(/:\d\d GMT/, " UTC");
---
<Base title="About & help" nav="about">
  <div class="container container--narrow">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>About &amp; help</h1>
      <p>A personal study site for the MuleSoft (Mule 4) course: the full lecture, a short summary podcast and three levels of notes for every lesson.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>How to study a lesson</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><b>Simple notes</b> (5 min) — know what's coming.</li>
        <li><b>Lecture</b> — watch the full class with the <b>Detailed notes</b> open.</li>
        <li><b>Slides</b> — the exact screens from the class, with timestamps into the video.</li>
        <li><b>Super-detailed notes</b> — the complete reference: demos, troubleshooting, interview Q&amp;A.</li>
        <li><b>Summary podcast</b> — revise the next day, or listen on a walk. Audio keeps playing while you browse the site.</li>
        <li><b>Revise</b> — the outline, Must Remember, Quick Recap, key terms and a self-test from the interview questions, all taken word-for-word from the notes.</li>
        <li>Press <b>Mark as Completed</b> when you're done.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Lesson status</h2>
      <p>A lesson is <b>not started</b> until you open it, <b>in progress</b> once you have opened it, and <b>completed</b> when you press <i>Mark as Completed</i>. The dashboard's <i>Recommended next</i> is the first unfinished lesson after your furthest completed one.</p>

      <h2>Search tips</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Results are grouped by lesson; <i>Also found in</i> links go straight to the other notes levels or slides that match.</li>
        <li>Use the chips to search only one kind of material, e.g. <i>Simple notes</i> for quick revision.</li>
        <li>Search covers note text, headings, code (including DataWeave) and slide captions. Words are matched by their start, so “handl” finds handler and handling.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Lecture vs. podcast</h2>
      <p>The <b>main lecture</b> is the original, full-length class on YouTube (often 1–2 hours). The <b>summary podcast</b> is a separate, much shorter recap (about 10–12 minutes) in two formats with the same content: a <b>video podcast</b> with slides or animation, and an <b>audio podcast</b>.</p>

      <h2>Your progress stays in this browser</h2>
      <p>Completed lessons, bookmarks, recently opened lessons, podcast positions, playback speed, reading progress and display settings are saved in this browser's local storage. There is no account: <b>progress does not sync between devices or browsers</b>, and clearing site data or using a private window resets it. On <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}my-study/`}>My study</a> you can download a backup file and restore it in another browser.</p>

      <h2>Offline</h2>
      <p>Pages and slide images you have already opened keep working without a connection (a notice appears at the top while you're offline). Lessons you haven't opened, search, lecture videos and podcasts need a connection — audio and video are never stored for offline use.</p>

      <h2>Keyboard</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><kbd>/</kbd> — search; in results, <kbd>↓</kbd> <kbd>↑</kbd> move between lessons</li>
        <li>Heading <kbd>#</kbd> links — copy a link to that section</li>
        <li><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> — move between links and buttons; all controls are keyboard-operable</li>
        <li>Slides viewer: <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd> to move, <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close</li>
        <li>Audio seek bar: <kbd>←</kbd> <kbd>→</kbd> when focused</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Listening on phones</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>The audio player stays at the bottom of the screen and keeps playing while you open other pages of this site.</li>
        <li>Lock-screen / notification controls (play, pause, skip) are provided where the browser supports the Media Session API (Chrome on Android, Safari on iOS 15+).</li>
        <li>Background playback with the screen off depends on the phone and browser. Android Chrome and iOS Safari normally continue; some browsers, battery savers or in-app browsers pause audio. If it stops, your position is saved — press play to continue.</li>
        <li>Install the site (browser menu → <i>Add to Home screen</i> / <i>Install app</i>) for a full-screen app-like window.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Content source</h2>
      <p>The notes and slides come unchanged from the <a href="https://github.com/developerashok99/green-c-mule-notes">green-c-mule-notes</a> repository{m.commit && <> (commit <code>{m.commit.slice(0, 7)}</code>)</>}, synchronised when this site was built ({synced}). The original notes website is at <a href="https://developerashok99.github.io/green-c-mule-notes/">developerashok99.github.io/green-c-mule-notes</a> and also has quizzes, flashcards and mind maps.</p>
      <p>Lecture video and podcast links are configured in <code>config/media.json</code> of the <a href="https://github.com/developerashok99/mule-learning-web">mule-learning-web</a> repository — see its README.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
